{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966061-little-gods","id":966061,"title":"Little Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T22:26:30-07:00","id":966061,"title":"Little Gods","content":"Has anyone every used the spirits and little gods from exalted in a WtA to &quot;fill out&quot; the Umbra?<br /> To clarify, CAN those be used with out a lot of &quot;dumbing down&quot;? Is what I am actually asking lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:30:37-07:00","id":966147,"title":"","content":"The Umbra is a complex spiritual ecosystem. I generally have the small spirits act as an early warning system. If they go quiet, it is a sign that something bad is in the area. I also use them as an immune system, they will attack anything weaker than them that enters the Umbra without protection (Mages without Spirit do not survive for very long in the Umbra in my games because they are swarmed by the small spirits if the Mage with Spirit in their group dies or abandons them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:04:50-07:00","id":966262,"title":"","content":"They would be somewhat incompatible with the way that spirits work in W:tA, since in Exalted, the god is not the river, but in Werewolf, the spirit of a river is its vital force and arguably even more important than the river.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:17:50-07:00","id":966459,"title":"","content":"Yes, and every object has a spirit, though the majority of spirits are asleep. That is the major difference between the small spirits of the Umbra and the little gods of Exalted. Even so, the Umbra should be populated by lots of small spirits who managed to survive the destruction of their habitat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T16:57:14-07:00","id":966487,"title":"","content":"Yeah I understand that everything has a spirit, and that 90% of those are slumbering. I also understand that the spiritual aspect of something/location is very vital. I was just wondering if it one tried to use the Little Gods of Exalted in WtA, would they need to be &quot;dumbed down&quot;. IMO the its just fluff where a Exalted Little God river spirit isn't actually the river. That can be tweaked to fit in. Its the power levels ok that I am conserned with. If it will take a lot of hammeri,g and twerking to use a Little God, then screw it lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:47:10-07:00","id":966501,"title":"","content":"Gnosis 1, Rage 1, Willpower 3, and Power 10 would probably be sufficient for small spirit (plus a few Charms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:57:42-07:00","id":966503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966061-little-gods?p=966501#post966501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gnosis 1, Rage 1, Willpower 3, and <b>Power 10</b> would probably be sufficient for small spirit (plus a few Charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Essence 5, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:00:56-07:00","id":966505,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out Yurgen Kaneko the Bull of the North is the past life of Yuri Konietzko the Shadowlord Legend. And I believe Scrags are the modern equivalent of Blood Apes. Like if say Blood Apes are Homo habilis then Scrags would be homo erectus. Blood apes are large muscular murder gorillas born and breed in Malfeas. Scrags are what we get after murder spirits have bred in the shadow of the world and its mortal cities for over an age, they've become slimmer, greyer and more man like.<br /> <br /> The thing is some things interact with physical Creation more often in Exalted, so many Elementals are harder to fit in. But oddly enough higher level spirits have an easier time fitting into Exalted. Demons in the Age of Sorrow could have stayed long enough to become Wyrm Totems in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness is more animistic then Exalted, so many of the Gods in Exalted would more translate to Totems/incarna in their connection to things. And Elementals perhaps are what evolved into things such as Mountain Spirits and River spirits as they embody what they are. Perhaps some little Gods become beings such as Fae and Hsien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:41:03-07:00","id":966637,"title":"","content":"Homo Erectus were nearly identical to Homo Sapiens, and you would not notice one as being exceptionally different than other humans if they were dressed in modern clothing. They were actually the most successful Homo species, as they survived for 1.5 million years before they evolved into Homo Sapiens. For all we know, they developed a thousand civilizations during their span, though anything more sophisticated than crude stone tools would have decayed within a few tens of thousands of years.<br /> <br /> The link between Exalted and the World of Darkness has been broken with 2nd edition and has been broken even further with 3rd edition. Anyway, it was a stupid idea that was just a poor marketing ploy to lure White Wolf fans to Exalted. At best, it is a Deep Umbra realm created by ancient entities that predate humanity.<br /> <br /> I really think that it is mechanically incorrect to draw correlations between the two worlds. The Changing Breeds have a history of 250 million years and predate humans by 248 million years. The spirits of WoD are just too different than the spirits of Exalted to create a correlation between the two gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:00:46-07:00","id":966644,"title":"","content":"Well I for one, aren't trying to draw a correlation between the two. I am just wanting to actually use some of them Little Gods as spirits in the Umbra, or in Domains. To spice things up if you will. If I were to use any of the Little Gods, any Exalted specifics for them would be removed and replaced with WoD specifics. <br /> <br /> Which is why I asked if one would have to &quot;dumb down&quot; Exalted Little Gods if one wanted to use them in WtA?<br /> <br /> Have no desire to link the two lines together. Have no interest in drawing correlations between them lol. I am just looking for additional encounter fodder already been made due to me working 70-80 hours a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:36:02-07:00","id":966704,"title":"","content":"The spirits of the Umbra have only four statistics: Gnosis, Rage, Willpower, and Power (or Chi). The Little God's have more. The fastest conversion would be to take the highest mental attribute and make Gnosis equal to that, take the highest physical attribute and make Rage equal to that, keep Willpower the same, give them Power (or Chi) 10, and give them a couple of Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:45:35-07:00","id":967017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966061-little-gods?p=966637#post966637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homo Erectus were nearly identical to Homo Sapiens, and you would not notice one as being exceptionally different than other humans if they were dressed in modern clothing. They were actually the most successful Homo species, as they survived for 1.5 million years before they evolved into Homo Sapiens. For all we know, they developed a thousand civilizations during their span, though anything more sophisticated than crude stone tools would have decayed within a few tens of thousands of years.<br /> <br /> The link between Exalted and the World of Darkness has been broken with 2nd edition and has been broken even further with 3rd edition. Anyway, it was a stupid idea that was just a poor marketing ploy to lure White Wolf fans to Exalted. At best, it is a Deep Umbra realm created by ancient entities that predate humanity.<br /> <br /> I really think that it is mechanically incorrect to draw correlations between the two worlds. The Changing Breeds have a history of 250 million years and predate humans by 248 million years. The spirits of WoD are just too different than the spirits of Exalted to create a correlation between the two gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put your species names in lower case, please. I don;t care about the italics, but non-generic names are in lower case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The spirits of the Umbra have only four statistics: Gnosis, Rage, Willpower, and Power (or Chi). The Little God's have more. The fastest conversion would be to take the highest mental attribute and make Gnosis equal to that, take the highest physical attribute and make Rage equal to that, keep Willpower the same, give them Power (or Chi) 10, and give them a couple of Charms.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> In Revised, Power/Chi was replaced with Essence, which is typically the sum of Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, but can vary with particularly weak or strong spirits (Nexus Crawlers and Dream Makers can have it higher, possibly as much as 300+ in the case of the latter). The costs that were in Power/Chi tend to be much reduced under the newer system, too, especially Materialize, which now costs nothing and just has a spirit using their normal traits, so long as their Gnosis is equal to or higher than the Gauntlet.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}